MuseScore Studio 4.7.6

The official x86_64 AppImage is obtained from:
https://github.com/musescore/MuseScore/releases/tag/v4.7.6
SOURCE.json identifies the release asset and its SHA-256. The executable,
AppRun launcher and bundled libraries are unmodified. solve.sh unpacks the
AppImage and replaces its example plugins, extensions and automation scripts
with empty directories. The separate musescore_start.py launcher initializes
the profile and retries one early desktop startup crash; it is not upstream
MuseScore code.

LICENSE contains the upstream GPL-3.0-only text and its font exception.
LICENSES contains the unmodified component notices extracted from the AppImage,
including MS Basic and the updater's libraries. The installed runtime also
retains these notices in its original share/doc and updater directories.
Bundled components retain their own licenses, including Qt and the soundfont.

Corresponding MuseScore source is tag v4.7.6, commit
96480d58445e3b24b230a3fe7d4725d639aa2eb3, of:
https://github.com/musescore/MuseScore
https://github.com/musescore/MuseScore/archive/refs/tags/v4.7.6.tar.gz
The source tag includes the build configuration for this release. Component
notices identify their respective upstream sources; Qt 6.10.2 source is
available from https://download.qt.io/archive/qt/6.10/6.10.2/single/ .

This distribution is not affiliated with or endorsed by MuseScore Limited.

process_guard.c is a separate runtime boundary, compiled at installation. It
uses Linux Landlock to confine writes and child-process execution. It does not
modify upstream application files.
